From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:32:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: samsung: exynos-pmu: add Google gs201 compatible

The gs201 (Tensor G2) PMU matches gs101: same secure register access
through SMC and the same CPU inform and interrupt generator layout.
Reuse the gs101 data.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c b/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c
index c764f35fb..1e7769db9 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c
@@ -125,6 +125,9 @@ static const struct of_device_id exynos_pmu_of_device_ids[] = {
 	{
 		.compatible = "google,gs101-pmu",
 		.data = &gs101_pmu_data,
+	}, {
+		.compatible = "google,gs201-pmu",
+		.data = &gs101_pmu_data,
 	}, {
 		.compatible = "samsung,exynos3250-pmu",
 		.data = exynos_pmu_data_arm_ptr(exynos3250_pmu_data),
